{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSc2bEMyrCRXQzA1YEyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create my analysis summary:\n\n**Requirement (restated):**\nAdd `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that changes an `ACTIVE` order to `CANCELLED`, cancels its `CREATED` shipments, handles idempotency for already-cancelled orders, rejects 409 if any shipment is `CONFIRMED`, rejects 404 for non-existent orders, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model (Order.kt:11): lacks status field; currently has orderId, customerId, amount, currency\n- Shipment model (Shipment.kt:9): already has status field with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:1-46): has create/getById/list; no cancel endpoint\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:1-56): has create/getById/list\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:1-27): in-memory store; no method to find shipments by orderId\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:1-27): in-memory store; no method to find by orderId\n- ApiExceptions (ApiExceptions.kt): ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Exception-based error handling: throw ApiException subclass, GlobalExceptionHandler produces envelope\n- ErrorCode enum for all machine-readable errors\n- All error responses use {error: {code, message, fields}} shape\n- Controllers inject repositories and call their methods\n- 409 ConflictException for state conflicts, 404 ResourceNotFoundException for missing resources\n- Order creation returns 201 CREATED\n- Tests use MockMvc, validate both status and response body (error envelope shape)\n- Tests reset repositories with @BeforeEach\n- Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for in-memory store\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - MUST add status field (OrderStatus enum like ShipmentStatus)\n2. OrderController.kt - MUST add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - MUST add findByOrderId() method for cancel logic\n4. OrderRepository.kt - may need updates to support cancel\n5. ApiError.kt - MUST add ORDER_CANCELLED or similar error codes\n6. ShipmentController.kt - MUST reject shipment create if order is CANCELLED (check before save)\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt - MUST add cancel endpoint tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding status field to Order changes GET /orders response shape; existing tests may fail if not updated\n- Cancellation must be all-or-nothing (transactional); in-memory store requires careful ordering\n- Cross-repository coordination: OrderController must check ShipmentRepository\n- New field in response might break clients expecting exact field set\n\n**Open questions:** None preventing progress - ShipmentStatus pattern establishes OrderStatus should be enum.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field (default ACTIVE on creation). Create `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Update `data class Order` to include status parameter.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `cancel()` method mapped to `POST /{orderId}/cancel`. Method: get order, throw 404 if not found, throw 409 (ConflictException) if any shipment of that order has status CONFIRMED, otherwise set order status to CANCELLED, update shipment statuses to CANCELLED for all CREATED shipments of that order, save and return the cancelled order. Before creating an order, initialize status to ACTIVE.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order (used by cancel logic).\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In `create()` method, check if the order exists; throw 409 ConflictException if order status is CANCELLED. This requires injecting OrderRepository and checking order status before saving shipment.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for when trying to create shipment on cancelled order) and `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL` (for when trying to cancel order with confirmed shipment). Alternatively, use existing `ORDER_CONFLICT` or single conflict message. Actually, looking at the requirement, the 409 for confirmed shipment should use a clear code. Let me add `ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` or similar.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order → 200, returns order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel active order → its CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order → 200, idempotent, no change\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, nothing changes\n   - Cancel non-existent order → 404\n   \n   Also add test that shipments are NOT cancelled if status is CONFIRMED.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test: creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order → 409 ConflictException.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could put all cancel logic in a service layer (OrderService) instead of controller, but existing codebase has no service layer and controllers call repositories directly. Keeping it in controller maintains consistency.\n- Could make order creation accept optional status parameter, but no reason to; always start ACTIVE.\n- Could use a single error code for all cancellation conflicts instead of specific ones, but being explicit in error codes (ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT vs ORDER_CANCELLED) helps clients understand what went wrong.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order** (happy path):\n   - Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n   - Get order from repository\n   - Query all shipments by orderId (new repository method)\n   - Check: if any shipment.status == CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException (409)\n   - For each shipment with status CREATED → save with status CANCELLED\n   - Save order with status CANCELLED\n   - Return: 200 OK with Order object (status=CANCELLED)\n\n2. **Cancel already-CANCELLED order** (idempotent):\n   - Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n   - Get order from repository\n   - Order.status is already CANCELLED\n   - Query shipments by orderId\n   - No CONFIRMED shipments (no exception thrown)\n   - Save order (no change)\n   - Return: 200 OK with Order object (status=CANCELLED)\n\n3. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment** (rejected, all-or-nothing):\n   - Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n   - Get order from repository\n   - Query shipments by orderId\n   - Find shipment with status CONFIRMED\n   - Throw ConflictException with code ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT (409)\n   - Neither order nor shipments are modified\n   - Return: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order**:\n   - Input: POST /orders/O-missing/cancel\n   - Get order from repository → null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404) with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - Return: 404 Not Found with error envelope\n\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**:\n   - Input: POST /shipments with orderId of cancelled order\n   - Get order from OrderRepository\n   - Order.status is CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException with code ORDER_CANCELLED (409)\n   - Shipment not created\n   - Return: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest:\n1. `cancel_active_order_returns_cancelled` - Create order, call cancel, verify 200, verify status=CANCELLED\n2. `cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments` - Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify shipment status changed to CANCELLED\n3. `cancel_active_order_does_not_cancel_confirmed_shipments` - Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment (or write directly to repo), cancel order, verify returns 409, verify shipment still CONFIRMED\n4. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` - Create order, cancel it, cancel it again, verify 200 and idempotent\n5. `cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404` - Call cancel on non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n6. `cancel_order_rejects_if_any_shipment_confirmed` - Create order with mixed shipments (CREATED and CONFIRMED), call cancel, verify 409 and nothing changed\n\nShipmentControllerTest:\n1. `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` - Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2647,"cache_read_input_tokens":21240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2647},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc451d05-8d0d-46bf-ba95-cacee775e9b1","uuid":"363b3731-eb82-4d64-a9f5-f63ef921ba20","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:30:08.372Z","request_id":"req_011CfSc2aRzC6CMNC8c5egsv"}
